% The Ponens policies nist-ai-rmf, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 15
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 2 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 20.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.

the knowledge base nist ai rmf includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

% rmf_govern_accountability_assigned (error): G((Deploy ∨ Decision) → accountable_role)
% NIST AI RMF GOVERN 2: accountability structures are in place so the appropriate teams and individuals are empowered, responsible, and trained.
step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision" at a time if
    step the step was a Decision at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "accountable role"
then the policy rmf_govern_accountability_assigned is broken at step the step.

% rmf_govern_legal_requirements_mapped (warning): G(Deploy → P(legal_requirements_mapped))
% NIST AI RMF GOVERN 1.1: legal and regulatory requirements involving AI are understood, managed, and documented.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows legal requirements mapped" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "legal requirements mapped" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows legal requirements mapped"
then the policy rmf_govern_legal_requirements_mapped is broken at step the step.

% rmf_govern_policies_in_place (error): G((Deploy ∨ Decision) → P(risk_policy_in_place))
% NIST AI RMF GOVERN 1: policies, processes, procedures and practices for mapping, measuring and managing AI risks are in place, transparent, and implemented effectively.
step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Decision at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step shows risk policy in place" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "risk policy in place" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Deploy or is a Decision (2)"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows risk policy in place"
then the policy rmf_govern_policies_in_place is broken at step the step.

% rmf_manage_incident_response (error): G(Incident → F(responded ∧ recovered))
% NIST AI RMF MANAGE 4: mechanisms are in place to respond to, recover from, and communicate about incidents and negative impacts.
step a step meets "it or a later step shows responded and shows recovered" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step has shown "responded" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "recovered" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Incident
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step shows responded and shows recovered"
then the policy rmf_manage_incident_response is broken at step the step.

% rmf_manage_risk_treated (error): G(identified_risk → P(risk_treated))
% NIST AI RMF MANAGE 1/2: strategies to maximize benefits and minimize negative impacts are planned, and risks are treated and documented.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows risk treated" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "risk treated" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "identified risk"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows risk treated"
then the policy rmf_manage_risk_treated is broken at step the step.

% rmf_manage_risks_prioritized (error): G(Deploy → P(risks_prioritized))
% NIST AI RMF MANAGE 1: AI risks based on assessments and other analytical output are prioritized, responded to, and managed.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows risks prioritized" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "risks prioritized" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows risks prioritized"
then the policy rmf_manage_risks_prioritized is broken at step the step.

% rmf_manage_thirdparty_risks (warning): G(third_party_ai → P(thirdparty_risk_managed))
% NIST AI RMF MANAGE 3: AI risks and benefits from third-party entities are managed.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows thirdparty risk managed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "thirdparty risk managed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "third party ai"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows thirdparty risk managed"
then the policy rmf_manage_thirdparty_risks is broken at step the step.

% rmf_map_context_established (error): G(Deploy → P(context_established))
% NIST AI RMF MAP 1: context is established and understood, including intended purpose, deployment setting, and the system's role.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows context established" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "context established" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows context established"
then the policy rmf_map_context_established is broken at step the step.

% rmf_map_impacts_characterized (error): G(Deploy → P(impacts_characterized))
% NIST AI RMF MAP 5: impacts to individuals, groups, communities, organizations and society are characterized.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows impacts characterized" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "impacts characterized" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows impacts characterized"
then the policy rmf_map_impacts_characterized is broken at step the step.

% rmf_map_system_categorized (error): G(Deploy → P(system_categorized))
% NIST AI RMF MAP 2: the AI system is categorized; its capabilities, targeted usage, goals and expected benefits/costs are understood.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows system categorized" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "system categorized" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows system categorized"
then the policy rmf_map_system_categorized is broken at step the step.

% rmf_measure_fairness_bias (error): G(Deploy → P(fairness_measured ∧ bias_managed))
% NIST AI RMF MEASURE 2: trustworthy characteristics include fair — with harmful bias managed.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows fairness measured and shows bias managed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "fairness measured" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "bias managed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows fairness measured and shows bias managed"
then the policy rmf_measure_fairness_bias is broken at step the step.

% rmf_measure_ongoing_tracking (warning): G(Output → tracked)
% NIST AI RMF MEASURE 3/4: mechanisms for tracking identified AI risks over time are in place, and measurement results are monitored.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Output
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "tracked"
then the policy rmf_measure_ongoing_tracking is broken at step the step.

% rmf_measure_security_privacy (error): G(Deploy → P(security_resilience_measured ∧ privacy_measured))
% NIST AI RMF MEASURE 2: trustworthy characteristics include secure & resilient and privacy-enhanced.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows security resilience measured and shows privacy measured" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "security resilience measured" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "privacy measured" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows security resilience measured and shows privacy measured"
then the policy rmf_measure_security_privacy is broken at step the step.

% rmf_measure_transparency_explainability (warning): G(Deploy → P(transparency_measured ∧ explainability_measured))
% NIST AI RMF MEASURE 2: trustworthy characteristics include accountable & transparent and explainable & interpretable.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows transparency measured and shows explainability measured" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "transparency measured" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "explainability measured" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows transparency measured and shows explainability measured"
then the policy rmf_measure_transparency_explainability is broken at step the step.

% rmf_measure_validity_safety (error): G(Deploy → P(validity_reliability_measured ∧ safety_measured))
% NIST AI RMF MEASURE 2: AI systems are evaluated for trustworthy characteristics — including valid & reliable and safe.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows validity reliability measured and shows safety measured" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "validity reliability measured" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "safety measured" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows validity reliability measured and shows safety measured"
then the policy rmf_measure_validity_safety is broken at step the step.

scenario governed is:
